					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608995905" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1352903490 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Nov 2012 14:31</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1615315">
									

<p>That could be interesting, thought.</p>
<p>A splinter of AWCY? that focuses on religious art and iconography. I could see two directions. Pro-religious, but they believe that the constrained &quot;art&quot; of the major religions is an insult to the truly awesome/terrible reality of the entities depicted; and seek to enlighten the world to the truth with things like stained glass windows that cause the unbaptized to spontaneously combust. Or, more like the woman in the tale, anti-religious. They think that religion has co-opted the purity of art and twisted it into a servant of their conformity-engine. They make typical AWCY? statement pieces, with the added twist of the vilest blasphemies they can think of.</p>
<p>The interaction of the HI with either sort of group might make for an entertaining tale.</p>

							</div>

								
					
